Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: discard power-save loopbacks after wakeup

A station wakeup drains its power-save queue once, while the frames
redirected by the PSE can still be waiting on a different RX ring. If
those loopbacks are processed after the wakeup, they are queued for an
already awake station and set the driver's buffered indication again.

Check ps_sleeping under ps_lock before buffering a loopback, and keep
the buffered notification in the same critical section. The wakeup's
state change and queue drain use that lock too, so a late frame cannot
repopulate the queue or publish a stale buffered indication after them.

Discard late frames instead of retransmitting their old sequence and
packet numbers after newer traffic or a wakeup BAR. The hardware pending
count is already settled when the loopback is received. Sleeping stations
still retain the existing frame parsing, queue limit and service-period
handling, including temporary hardware PS bypass during U-APSD.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/mt7603/dma.c b/mt7603/dma.c
--- a/mt7603/dma.c
+++ b/mt7603/dma.c
@@ -93,7 +93,6 @@
 	}
 
 	skb->priority = tid;
-	ieee80211_sta_set_buffered(sta, tid, true);
 
 	val = le32_to_cpu(txd[0]);
 	val &= ~(MT_TXD0_P_IDX | MT_TXD0_Q_IDX);
@@ -101,6 +100,13 @@
 	txd[0] = cpu_to_le32(val);
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->ps_lock);
+	/* The wake-up may have drained psq before this loopback arrived. */
+	if (!msta->ps_sleeping) {
+		spin_unlock_bh(&dev->ps_lock);
+		goto free;
+	}
+
+	ieee80211_sta_set_buffered(sta, tid, true);
 	__skb_queue_tail(&msta->psq, skb);
 	if (skb_queue_len(&msta->psq) >= MT7603_PSQ_MAX) {
 		skb = __skb_dequeue(&msta->psq);
